WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.070
A pencil moves across lined
paper, in big careful letters:

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.680
mum sed we can go.

3
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.710
A red pen swoops down
on sed, ready to fix it.

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.110
Then it stops.

5
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.850
Is this a mistake to correct,
or a sign that she's learning?

6
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.630
Why would a six-year-old write sed?

7
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.060
In this mission, you'll see how
six-year-olds are taught to read in the first

8
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.040
place, with phonics.

9
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.350
You'll climb the stages of early writing,

10
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.720
from scribble to correct spelling.

11
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.450
And you'll read a beach
story by a boy of six,

12
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.960
full of clues.

13
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.350
Your mission: decide
whether 'sed' is progress,

14
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.700
and explain why.
